# Normalise line endings across Windows, macOS and Linux.
#
# Windows ends a line with CRLF, macOS and Linux with LF. Without this file,
# a Mac user saving a file a Windows user wrote can make Git report that every
# line changed — turning a three-line fix into a whole-file diff that nobody
# can review. This has nothing to do with the code being wrong; it is purely
# how the bytes are stored.
#
# `text=auto` tells Git: store LF in the repository, and convert to whatever
# the checking-out machine prefers. Everyone edits normally; the repository
# stays consistent.
* text=auto

# Explicit, so intent survives even if the auto-detection is ever wrong.
*.py    text diff=python
*.md    text
*.txt   text
*.json  text
*.html  text
*.css   text
*.js    text
*.yml   text
*.yaml  text
*.cfg   text
*.ini   text
*.sh    text eol=lf

# Binary — never convert these, it would corrupt them.
*.xlsx  binary
*.xls   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.docx  binary
*.pptx  binary
